2001 CRI.L.J 4745 (Supreme Court), between K.N.Beena Vs. Muniyappan, it is held that;
" Negotiable Instrument Act -S- 138, 139, 118- cheque dishonour complaint- Burden of proving that cheque had not been issued for any debt or liability - is on the accused - Denial/averments in reply by accused are not sufficient to shift burden of proof on to the complainant- Accused has to prove in trail by leading cogent evidence that there was no debt or liability - setting Crl.A.No.1323/2023 aside conviction on basis of some formal evidence led by accused - Not proper. "
